From: Baochen Qiang <baochen.qiang@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:34:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: synchronize MLO peer links and deletion lifetime

ath12k_mac_vdev_create() for an AP vdev creates the bss self-peer via
ath12k_peer_create(), which finishes by calling
ath12k_dp_link_peer_assign() to publish the dp_link_peer in the
dp_hw->dp_peers[peerid_index] RCU table, in the dp_peer's link_peers[]
array, and in the per-addr rhashtable.

ath12k_peer_mlo_link_peers_delete() sends WMI peer_delete for every link
before waiting for any peer_unmap / peer_delete_resp event. The shared per-
radio completion ar->peer_delete_done could not disambiguate which peer a
response was for: every call to ath12k_peer_delete_send() did
reinit_completion(&ar->peer_delete_done), so when an event for the first
link arrived between two sends it raised the count to 1 and the second send
promptly cleared it; the wait for the second link then timed out with

The TX control link field can contain zero for MLD frames even when link
zero is not part of the VIF. ath12k treats that value as an explicit link,
fails to find an arvif and drops the frame.

The ahvif link pointer array is protected by RCU whereas links_map is not.
During link removal, clearing a link pointer before links_map leaves a
window where readers see the old bitmap but dereference a NULL arvif.

